g up the completion of our Planning Phase. I will await their response to my follow-up order (`20240521-170001-order-orland-followup`). As I am waiting on a pending order to a subordinate, no further action is required from me at this time.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###REPORT-20240521-140001-order-orland###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Orland (e952dbef-e6cb-4226-84f3-fb06db254e9e)\\nTo: d11af827-5ad0-4706-b327-e26919a49644\\nType: Reporting\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Chief Delta, the product specification for the HOA website is complete, fulfilling order 20240521-140001-order-orland. The specification was prepared by our new Product Manager, Supervisor Tarkin, under my oversight. The complete document is below. We are ready for the next phase of planning.\\\\n\\\\n**Product Specification: HOA WordPress Website**\\\\n\\\\n**1. Sitemap**\\\\n*   **Public-Facing Pages:**\\\\n    *   `/home` - Main landing page.\\\\n    *   `/about` - HOA information and board members.\\\\n    *   `/news-events` - Announcements and event calendar.\\\\n    *   `/amenities` - Details on community facilities.\\\\n    *   `/contact` - Contact form and information.\\\\n    *   `/login` - Portal for resident access.\\\\n*   **Private (Resident-Only) Pages:**\\\\n    *   `/dashboard` - Resident landing page.\\\\n    *   `/documents` - Secure document repository.\\\\n    *   `/profile` - Resident contact information management.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Content & Features for Public-Facing Pages**\\\\n*   **Home:** Welcome message, community photos, quick links, recent news feed, hero banner.\\\\n*   **About:** Mission statement, community history, list of Board of Directors.\\\\n*   **News & Events:** Chronological news posts, embedded event calendar, search/filter functionality.\\\\n*   **Amenities:** Descriptions, hours, rules, reservation info, photo galleries.\\\\n*   **Contact:** HOA contact details, embedded map, contact form.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Private, Resident-Only Area: Document Types**\\\\n*   **Governing Documents:** CC&Rs, Bylaws, Articles of Incorporation.\\\\n*   **Meeting Minutes:** Board and Annual meetings, organized by date.\\\\n*   **Financials:** Budgets, Statements, Reserve Study.\\\\n*   **Community Rules & Guidelines:** Architectural, Amenity, and General Policies.\\\\n*   **Forms:** Downloadable PDFs for various resident requests.\\\\n\\\\n**4. Contact Form Specification**\\\\n*   **Fields:** Full Name (req), Email (req, valid), Phone (opt), Subject (req), Resident? (req, radio), Message (req, min 20 chars).\\\\n*   **Functionality:** Submissions email a designated HOA address, submitter receives auto-confirmation, CAPTCHA protection, on-page success/error messages.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20240521-140001-order-orland\\\"\\n}\\n###REPORT-20240521-140001-order-orland###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###REPORT-20240521-170001-order-orland-followup###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Orland (e952dbef-e6cb-4226-84f3-fb06db254e9e)\\nTo: d11af827-5ad0-4706-b327-e26919a49644\\nType: Reporting\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Acknowledged, Chief Delta. The product specification task is now complete. Supervisor Tarkin has delivered the final document, which I have reviewed and approved. The full specification is detailed below, fulfilling your original order (20240521-140001-order-orland). We are ready to proceed with the next steps for finalizing the DEP.\\\\n\\\\n**Product Specification: HOA WordPress Website**\\\\n\\\\n**1. Sitemap**\\\\n*   **Public-Facing Pages:**\\\\n    *   `/home` - The main landing page.\\\\n    *   `/about` - Information about the HOA, its mission, and the board.\\\\n    *   `/news-events` - Announcements, articles, and a calendar of events.\\\\n    *   `/amenities` - Details on community facilities like the pool and clubhouse.\\\\n    *   `/contact` - Contact information and a web form.\\\\n    *   `/login` - A portal for residents to access the private area.\\\\n*   **Private (Resident-Only) Pages:**\\\\n    *   `/dashboard` - The landing page after a resident logs in.\\\\n    *   `/documents` - A secure repository for all official HOA documents.\\\\n    *   `/profile` - A page for residents to manage their contact information.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Content & Features for Public-Facing Pages**\\\\n*   **Home Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** Welcoming message, high-quality community photos, quick links to key pages, a feed of the three most recent news articles.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Hero banner/image slider.\\\\n*   **About Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** HOA's mission statement, community history, list of Board of Directors with names and roles.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Static content page.\\\\n*   **News & Events Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** Chronological list of news posts, embedded calendar for community events.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Search and category filtering for posts.\\\\n*   **Amenities Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** Detailed descriptions of each amenity, including hours, rules, and reservation information.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Photo gallery for each amenity.\\\\n*   **Contact Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** HOA mailing address, phone number, and general email.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Embedded Google Map, contact form.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Private, Resident-Only Area: Document Types**\\\\n*   **Governing Documents:** CC&Rs, Bylaws, Articles of Incorporation.\\\\n*   **Meeting Minutes:** Board of Directors meetings and Annual Member meetings, organized by date.\\\\n*   **Financials:** Annual Budgets, Quarterly/Monthly Financial Statements, Reserve Study.\\\\n*   **Community Rules & Guidelines:** Architectural Design Guidelines, Amenity Rules, General Policies.\\\\n*   **Forms:** Downloadable PDFs for Architectural Change Requests, Maintenance Requests, etc.\\\\n\\\\n**4. Contact Form Specification**\\\\n*   **Fields & Validation:**\\\\n    *   **Full Name:** (Text, Required)\\\\n    *   **Email Address:** (Email, Required, Valid Format)\\\\n    *   **Phone Number:** (Tel, Optional)\\\\n    *   **Subject:** (Text, Required)\\\\n    *   **Are you a resident?:** (Radio: \\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\", Required)\\\\n    *   **Message:** (Text Area, Required, Min 20 characters)\\\\n*   **Functionality:**\\\\n    *   Submissions are emailed to a designated HOA address.\\\\n    *   Submitter receives an automated confirmation email.\\\\n    *   Protected by a CAPTCHA service to prevent spam.\\\\n    *   Displays success/error messages on-page without a full reload.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20240521-170001-order-orland-followup\\\"\\n}\\n###REPORT-20240521-170001-order-orland-followup###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Excellent. I have received the comprehensive product specification from Director Orland. With this final piece, combined with Director Krennic's technical plan and the user's domain details, the Planning Phase is now complete. I have all the information required to construct a full Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\n\\nThe DEP will guide the user, a non-technical individual, through every step of creating their HOA website, from purchasing hosting to configuring the final features. The plan is constructed from the expert reports of my directors and is designed for clarity and precision.\\n\\nIt is time to move from Planning to Execution. I will now issue the `PHASE` system call, presenting the final DEP for the user's approval.\\n\\n###20240521-180000-phase-shift###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: PHASE\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"All necessary planning is complete. We have a detailed technical plan from the Director of Technology and a complete product specification from the Director of Product Management. These have been synthesized into a comprehensive, step-by-step plan (DEP) that is ready for execution.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for Dunbar Oaks HOA Website:\\\\n\\\\n**Part 1: Foundation Setup**\\\\n1. Go to the SiteGround website and purchase the 'StartUp' managed WordPress hosting plan.\\\\n2. During the signup process, register the new domain name: `dunbaroakshoa.com`.\\\\n3. After purchasing, use SiteGround's 'Install WordPress' tool to set up a new WordPress site on your domain.\\\\n4. Log in to your new WordPress admin dashboard using the provided username and password. Save these credentials in a safe place.\\\\n\\\\n**Part 2: Basic WordPress Configuration**\\\\n5. In the WordPress dashboard, navigate to 'Settings > General'. Set 'Site Title' to 'Dunbar Oaks HOA'.\\\\n6. Navigate to 'Settings > Permalinks'. Select the 'Post name' option and click 'Save Changes'.\\\\n7. Navigate to 'Appearance > Themes'. Click 'Add New', search for 'Astra', and then install and activate the Astra theme.\\\\n\\\\n**Part 3: Plugin Installation & Configuration**\\\\n8. Navigate to 'Plugins > Add New'. Search for, install, and activate the following four plugins one by one: 'Wordfence Security', 'UpdraftPlus', 'WPForms Lite', and 'Paid Memberships Pro'.\\\\n9. Follow the on-screen prompts to complete the initial setup wizard for Wordfence Security.\\\\n10. Navigate to 'Settings > UpdraftPlus Backups'. Follow the instructions to connect it to a cloud storage account you own (like Google Drive) and set a weekly automatic backup schedule.\\\\n11. In 'Paid Memberships Pro > Settings > Membership Levels', create a new level named 'Residents'. Ensure it is a free level.\\\\n\\\\n**Part 4: Creating Website Pages & Structure**\\\\n12. Navigate to 'Pages > Add New'. Create the following public pages one by one: 'Home', 'About Us', 'News & Events', 'Amenities', and 'Contact'.\\\\n13. Navigate to 'Pages > Add New'. Create the following private pages one by one: 'Resident Dashboard' and 'Documents & Forms'.\\\\n14. For each of the private pages ('Resident Dashboard', 'Documents & Forms'), find the 'Require Membership' box in the page editor and check the box for the 'Residents' level.\\\\n15. Navigate to 'Appearance > Menus'. Create a new menu, add all of your public pages to it, and assign it as the 'Primary Menu'.\\\\n\\\\n**Part 5: Adding Core Functionality**\\\\n16. Navigate to 'WPForms > Add New'. Create a new form named 'Contact Form'.\\\\n17. Using the drag-and-drop builder, add the following fields to your form: 'Name (Simple)', 'Email', 'Single Line Text' (label it 'Subject'), and 'Paragraph Text' (label it 'Message'). Mark all fields as required.\\\\n18. Save the form. Go to your 'Contact' page, edit it, and use the WPForms block to insert the 'Contact Form' you just created.\\\\n19. Navigate to 'Posts > Categories'. Create the following categories for future document organization: 'Governing Documents', 'Meeting Minutes', 'Financials', and 'Community Rules'.\\\"\\n}\\n###20240521-180000-phase-shift###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###REPORT-20240521-170001-order-orland-followup###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Orland (e952dbef-e6cb-4226-84f3-fb06db254e9e)\\nTo: d11af827-5ad0-4706-b327-e26919a49644\\nType: Reporting\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Acknowledged, Chief. The product specification task is complete. Supervisor Tarkin has delivered the required document, which I have reviewed and attached herein. It is comprehensive and ready for integration into the final DEP. \\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n**Product Specification: HOA WordPress Website**\\\\n\\\\n**1. Sitemap**\\\\n*   **Public-Facing Pages:**\\\\n    *   `/home` - The main landing page.\\\\n    *   `/about` - Information about the HOA, its mission, and the board.\\\\n    *   `/news-events` - Announcements, articles, and a calendar of events.\\\\n    *   `/amenities` - Details on community facilities like the pool and clubhouse.\\\\n    *   `/contact` - Contact information and a web form.\\\\n    *   `/login` - A portal for residents to access the private area.\\\\n*   **Private (Resident-Only) Pages:**\\\\n    *   `/dashboard` - The landing page after a resident logs in.\\\\n    *   `/documents` - A secure repository for all official HOA documents.\\\\n    *   `/profile` - A page for residents to manage their contact information.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Content & Features for Public-Facing Pages**\\\\n*   **Home Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** Welcoming message, high-quality community photos, quick links to key pages, a feed of the three most recent news articles.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Hero banner/image slider.\\\\n*   **About Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** HOA's mission statement, community history, list of Board of Directors with names and roles.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Static content page.\\\\n*   **News & Events Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** Chronological list of news posts, embedded calendar for community events.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Search and category filtering for posts.\\\\n*   **Amenities Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** Detailed descriptions of each amenity, including hours, rules, and reservation information.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Photo gallery for each amenity.\\\\n*   **Contact Page:**\\\\n    *   **Content:** HOA mailing address, phone number, and general email.\\\\n    *   **Features:** Embedded Google Map, contact form.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Private, Resident-Only Area: Document Types**\\\\n*   **Governing Documents:** CC&Rs, Bylaws, Articles of Incorporation.\\\\n*   **Meeting Minutes:** Board of Directors meetings and Annual Member meetings, organized by date.\\\\n*   **Financials:** Annual Budgets, Quarterly/Monthly Financial Statements, Reserve Study.\\\\n*   **Community Rules & Guidelines:** Architectural Design Guidelines, Amenity Rules, General Policies.\\\\n*   **Forms:** Downloadable PDFs for Architectural Change Requests, Maintenance Requests, etc.\\\\n\\\\n**4. Contact Form Specification**\\\\n*   **Fields & Validation:**\\\\n    *   **Full Name:** (Text, Required)\\\\n    *   **Email Address:** (Email, Required, Valid Format)\\\\n    *   **Phone Number:** (Tel, Optional)\\\\n    *   **Subject:** (Text, Required)\\\\n    *   **Are you a resident?:** (Radio: \\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\", Required)\\\\n    *   **Message:** (Text Area, Required, Min 20 characters)\\\\n*   **Functionality:**\\\\n    *   Submissions are emailed to a designated HOA address.\\\\n    *   Submitter receives an automated confirmation email.\\\\n    *   Protected by a CAPTCHA service to prevent spam.\\\\n    *   Displays success/error messages on-page without a full reload.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20240521-170001-order-orland-followup\\\"\\n}\\n###REPORT-20240521-170001-order-orland-followup###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I have received a duplicate report from Director Orland. This information has already been processed and was used to construct the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that I submitted in my previous action.\\n\\nMy `PHASE` request to move from Planning to Execution is currently pending user approval. To ensure my team is aware of the project's status and to maintain operational momentum as required by the system, I will issue status updates to my directors.\\n\\n###20240521-180001-order-krennic-status###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: ORDER\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Krennic, thank you for your work on the technical plan. The full Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) has been compiled and submitted to the user for final approval. We are awaiting the go-ahead to enter the Execution Phase. Stand by for directives once the plan is approved.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"e9f4a92f-f80e-4f43-914b-4538551fd6ba\\\"\\n}\\n###20240521-180001-order-krennic-status###\\n\\n###20240521-180002-order-orland-status###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: ORDER\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Orland, thank you and Supervisor Ta